qualification_3e1f1105: TF_GLM_EXL3_PGROUP, the parallel grouping of bertholomus (Albert Lee, BertholomusAI;
https://github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, branch glm-dsa-tp4, commit dbe0773 "perf(exl3 experts): prompt chunks decode
each weight tile once for up to 64 member rows", Apache-2.0; his commits name Claude Opus 5.5 as co-author): his
experts.cu lines 74-145 (PLACE_THREADS, block_sum, group_count_kernel, group_place_kernel) inserted after
group_kernel, unchanged. group_count_kernel counts each expert's members (a 256-thread block an expert);
group_place_kernel puts each used expert at its place in id order and lists its members in row order with the same
(i / slots) * 32 + (i % slots) encoding, -1 after the last up to maxm: group_kernel's lists byte for byte, for any
number of rows (no shared-memory staging). python-0.6's experts.cu equals dbe0773's through line 73. exl3_copies.py
applies this hunk in memory to write exl3/experts.cu, and after exl3_x1.patch's hunks to write exl3/x1/experts.cu.

--- a/src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.cu
+++ b/src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.cu
@@ -69,6 +69,78 @@
         for (; j < maxm; ++j) members[place * maxm + j] = -1;
         ++place;
